how did miles teller get his facial  scars and what impact did the accident  that caused them have on his acting  career keep watching to find out  miles teller just has one of those faces  the actor has built an impressive resume  over the course of the past decade  starring in both blockbuster action  movies and character-driven independent  films in equal measure and while some  audiences might not have previously  recognized teller the long-awaited  sequel to 1986's top gun top gun  maverick has likely changed that teller  plays bradley rooster bradshaw the son  of pete maverick mitchells former radio  intercept officer best friend and  partner in crime nick goose bradshaw  played by anthony edwards in the  original film the resemblance between  these two unrelated actors is downright  eerie making tellers casting a fitting  choice teller made his feature film  debut in 2010's rabbit hole in which he  starred opposite nicole kidman in the  2011 remake of footloose he took on the  role of willard a good natured guy with  two left feet teller's breakout  performance was in the 2013 coming of  age drama the spectacular now which won  the special jury prize at the sundance  film festival and proved that teller  could hold his own as a leading man for  the first time some of his other film  credits include the oscar-nominated  whiplash the fantastic four and the  divergent trilogy given his wide-ranging  success as a performer it's hard to  believe there was once a time when  teller was turned away after auditions  because of his facial scars during an  interview with the abc news's popcorn  with peter travers teller revealed that  his face was wounded and subsequently  scarred during his young adulthood which  then affected his burgeoning acting  career when he was 20 years old and  attending college teller was injured in  a serious car accident after his friend  lost control of a vehicle while driving  at 80 miles per hour the car rolled  eight times in total and ejected teller  50 feet away we flipped like eight times  going 80 miles per hour and i actually  flew out my window after being thrown  from the vehicle the actor ended up in  such bad shape that his friend thought  he might be dead fortunately teller  survived the incident after sustaining  some significant injuries to his face  following the accident teller underwent  multiple painful surgeries to remove the  scar tissue resulting from his wounds  over the course of roughly four years as  it turns out he still has some pieces of  gravel embedded in his face which his  doctors said would cause even more  damage if removed rather than if left  alone for a while teller's appearance  after the car accident stood in the way  of his acting ambitions as he told abc  news when i first started auditioning  people were straight up just like yeah  miles is a good actor but it doesn't  make sense for this character to have  scars the scars used to be really bad  but i was very surprised about how  comfortable people felt just being like  man what happened to your face soon  however one director took a chance on  teller when others would not putting him  on the career trajectory he maintains  today as teller revealed in his  interview with peter travers rabbit hole  director john cameron mitchell didn't  just cast him in his debut feature in  spite of his facial scars instead the  director saw the scars as a strength  teller recounts mitchell characterizing  his scars as adding a new dimension to  his character in the film beyond the  mystique with which they imbue teller's  character in rabbit hole he portrays the  driver of a car that killed a young boy  in a happenstance accident so the  real-life source of his scars parallel  this fictional incident teller would  then go on to appear in the spectacular  now and whiplash both of which include  pivotal scenes in which teller's  character is involved in car accidents  so in the end rather than his facial  scars hindering him they seemingly  became part of his identity as an actor  as it turned out teller's scars helped  to shape him and led him to roles for  which this aspect of his appearance  became a unique strength of course  tyler's filmography isn't limited to  just films featuring car accidents as  evidenced by his marquee role in top gun  maverick when teller's casting was  announced back in 2018 he beat out both  nicholas holt and glenn powell alongside  whom he tested for the role it's safe to  say that at this stage teller is  unencumbered by his injuries and the  hardships it caused early on in his  career  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

